@*
    The one way this UI says "waiting for the server".

    Loading was previously written inline on every page, which drifted in size, wording, and whether
    aria-busy was set at all. Consolidating it means a screen reader announces a pending region the
    same way everywhere, and the spinner never competes with the content it is standing in for.

    Two variants, chosen by how much is unknown:
      Inline — one region of a rendered page is still resolving; sits in the flow at text size.
      Block  — the whole panel has nothing to show yet; centred, with room around it.

    Always indeterminate. A determinate bar would have to invent a percentage, and no call this UI
    makes reports progress. See docs/20 §3 on not faking progress.
*@

@*
    The Block variant carries the product's flight treatment; Inline keeps the compact spinner.
    That split is deliberate: a route drawing itself inside a one-line region would be noise, while
    a panel with nothing in it yet is exactly where the product's own visual language belongs.

    Both announce identically, so the choice is presentation only. SoFlightLoading owns its own
    role/aria-live, so this wrapper does not add a second live region around it.
*@
@if (Variant == LoadingVariant.Block)
{
    <div class="@CssClass">
        <SoFlightLoading Message="@Message" Bare="true" />
    </div>
}
else
{
    <div class="@CssClass" role="status" aria-busy="true" aria-live="polite">
        <MudProgressCircular Indeterminate="true" Size="@SpinnerSize" />
        <span class="so-loading-text">@Message</span>
    </div>
}

@code {
    /// <summary>How much of the surface is pending.</summary>
    public enum LoadingVariant
    {
        /// <summary>A region inside an otherwise rendered page.</summary>
        Inline,

        /// <summary>The whole panel, with nothing else to show yet.</summary>
        Block
    }

    /// <summary>
    /// What is being waited for, in the operator's terms ("Yetkileriniz doğrulanıyor…"), not the
    /// mechanism. This is announced to assistive technology, so it must stand alone.
    /// </summary>
    [Parameter, EditorRequired]
    public string Message { get; set; } = string.Empty;

    /// <summary>Layout to use. Defaults to the in-flow form.</summary>
    [Parameter]
    public LoadingVariant Variant { get; set; } = LoadingVariant.Inline;

    /// <summary>
    /// Set when the element already sits inside a panel, to avoid drawing a second border around it.
    /// </summary>
    [Parameter]
    public bool Bare { get; set; }

    private Size SpinnerSize => Variant == LoadingVariant.Block ? Size.Medium : Size.Small;

    private string CssClass => Variant switch
    {
        LoadingVariant.Block => "so-loading so-loading--block",
        _ => Bare ? "so-loading" : "so-panel so-loading"
    };
}
